<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Berar is a historical region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, now the western part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidarbha">Vidarbha</a> division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, around Amravati and Akola. A fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>-growing plain, it was a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a>, an independent sultanate from about 1490 to 1574, a Mughal province and then part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a>'s lands. The Nizam assigned it to the British in 1853, and it was later joined to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces</a>.</p></div>
